cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use StarNest, please cite the software below. If your use relates to our open-cluster study, also cite the working paper listed under references (it is not yet published, so it is not the preferred citation)."
title: "StarNest: Open-Source Web Pipeline for Open Star Cluster Photometry and Kinematics"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
abstract: >-
  StarNest takes a Gaia DR3 cone-search catalogue of an open cluster and returns Gaussian-mixture membership, extinction, a PARSEC
  isochrone fit, proper-motion and 3-D kinematics, a mass function compared with Salpeter, Kroupa and Chabrier, binary-aware stellar and
  cluster masses, and mass-segregation and tidal diagnostics. It runs as a web app, as Python modules and as a batch command line.
  The mass method is inspired by Almeida, Monteiro & Dias (2023) but is not a strict replication; see the README, section 9.
